  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0093_ba03d050df82.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 175px;\" /></p><p>The saturation zone and cut-off area are known as the transistor switch&rsquo;s working regions. This implies that, by switching between its &ldquo;top-off&rdquo; (saturation) and &ldquo;absolute OFF,&rdquo; the transistor is used as a switch.</p>"
